<section class="bg-white dark:bg-gray-950 py-20 border-t border-gray-100 dark:border-gray-800">
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="text-center mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100">
        What the Domain Checker API Does
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 max-w-2xl mx-auto">
        One endpoint. Everything you need to know about a domain — availability, ownership, and registration history.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-8">

      <!-- Accuracy block -->
      <div class="bg-white dark:bg-gray-800 rounded-xl shadow p-6">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100 mb-2">Accuracy</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 text-sm mb-4">
          Every response includes parsed WHOIS data (domain ownership and registration records), DNS status (whether traffic-routing records exist), SSL validity (active HTTPS certificate), MX records (mail server configuration), and a reputation score — all normalized into a consistent JSON structure.
        </p>
        <pre class="bg-gray-900 text-green-400 rounded-lg p-4 overflow-x-auto text-sm font-mono">{
  "domain":      "example.com",
  "status":      "active",
  "dns_records": true,
  "ssl_valid":   true,
  "mx_valid":    true,
  "reputation":  "clean"
}</pre>
      </div>

      <!-- Simplicity block -->
      <div class="bg-gray-50 dark:bg-gray-900 rounded-xl shadow p-6">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100 mb-2">Simplicity</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 text-sm mb-4">
          A single POST request with your API key is all it takes. No SDK, no configuration, no setup — just an HTTP call and a JSON response.
        </p>
        <pre class="bg-gray-900 text-green-400 rounded-lg p-4 overflow-x-auto text-sm font-mono">POST /api/v1/domain-checker
Host: api.requiems.xyz
X-API-Key: your_key
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "domain": "example.com"
}</pre>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>
